[\n  {\n    \"title\": \"New Windows 'MiniPlasma' zero-day exploit gives SYSTEM access, PoC released\",\n    \"published_at\": \"2026-05-17T18:30:00-04:00\",\n    \"summary\": \"A proof-of-concept exploit dubbed “MiniPlasma” was released for a Windows local privilege escalation issue reported as effectively resurfacing a previously assigned and supposedly fixed Cloud Filter driver vulnerability (CVE-2020-17103). Testing reported successful elevation to SYSTEM on fully patched Windows 11, raising concerns about patch regression or incomplete remediation.\",\n    \"impact\": \"Local attackers can escalate to SYSTEM, enabling full device takeover, credential dumping, and disabling security controls after initial foothold.\",\n    \"recommendation\": \"Reduce local code execution paths, monitor for exploit artifacts and abnormal Cf* API usage; prioritize mitigations until an official fix is confirmed.\",\n    \"sources\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"BleepingComputer\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/microsoft/new-windows-miniplasma-zero-day-exploit-gives-system-access-poc-released/\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"MSRC CVE-2020-17103\",\n        \"url\": \"https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2020-17103\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Nightmare-Eclipse GitHub\",\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/Nightmare-Eclipse\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"is_older_than_24h\": false\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"[+24h Old] Microsoft rejects critical Azure Backup for AKS vulnerability report, no CVE issued\",\n    \"published_at\": \"2026-05-16T16:55:00-04:00\",\n    \"summary\": \"A researcher claims an Azure Backup for AKS privilege escalation path allowed a low-privileged “Backup Contributor” role to trigger Trusted Access relationships and obtain cluster-admin privileges, while Microsoft disputes the severity and says it’s expected behavior. The report alleges observable post-disclosure behavior changes consistent with a silent fix and highlights the resulting defender visibility gap without a CVE.\",\n    \"impact\": \"If exploitable as described, could allow privilege escalation to cluster-admin and access to secrets/workload manipulation in AKS environments.\",\n    \"recommendation\": \"Audit Azure RBAC assignments to backup vaults and require explicit Trusted Access setup; monitor for unexpected backup enablement and privilege binding changes.\",\n    \"sources\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"BleepingComputer\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/microsoft-rejects-critical-azure-vulnerability-report-no-cve-issued/\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Research writeup\",\n        \"url\": \"http://olearysec.com/research/azure-backup-aks-silent-patch/\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"is_older_than_24h\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"[+24h Old] PoC code published for critical NGINX vulnerability (CVE-2026-42945)\",\n    \"published_at\": \"2026-05-16T06:02:00-04:00\",\n    \"summary\": \"Technical details and PoC code were published for CVE-2026-42945, a heap buffer overflow in NGINX’s rewrite module that can cause DoS and-under certain conditions such as disabled ASLR-potential RCE. The flaw was patched in updated NGINX open source and NGINX Plus releases, with researchers detailing exploitation mechanics including multi-pass processing state mismatch leading to undersized allocations.\",\n    \"impact\": \"High-risk for exposed NGINX deployments using vulnerable rewrite/set configurations; could enable service disruption and potentially code execution in weakened environments.\",\n    \"recommendation\": \"Patch NGINX immediately and review rewrite/set usage; ensure ASLR is enabled and reduce exposure of internet-facing instances.\",\n    \"sources\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"SecurityWeek\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.securityweek.com/poc-code-published-for-critical-nginx-vulnerability/\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Depthfirst research\",\n        \"url\": \"https://depthfirst.com/research/nginx-rift-achieving-nginx-rce-via-an-18-year-old-vulnerability\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"F5 advisory\",\n        \"url\": \"https://my.f5.com/manage/s/article/K000161019\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"is_older_than_24h\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"[+24h Old] Android 16 VPN bypass (“Tiny UDP Cannon”) lets apps reveal real IP address\",\n    \"published_at\": \"2026-05-16\",\n    \"summary\": \"Researchers describe a privacy-impacting Android 16 flaw where a normal app can register a QUIC close payload such that the privileged system_server later transmits attacker-controlled UDP traffic outside the VPN tunnel-even when Always-On VPN and “Block connections without VPN” are enabled. Google reportedly classified the issue as infeasible to fix, while mitigations include disabling the vulnerable QUIC feature via device_config.\",\n    \"impact\": \"Can de-anonymize VPN users by leaking real IP and transmit data outside VPN protections, enabling tracking and possible exfiltration.\",\n    \"recommendation\": \"Apply mitigations to disable the QUIC close payload feature where feasible and monitor for unexpected UDP egress bypassing VPN interfaces.\",\n    \"sources\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Cyber Security News\",\n        \"url\": \"https://cybersecuritynews.com/android-16-vpn-bypass/\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Lowlevel.fun\",\n        \"url\": \"https://lowlevel.fun/posts/tiny-udp-cannon-android-vpn-bypass/\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"is_older_than_24h\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"[+24h Old] Google Project Zero discloses zero-click exploit chain for Pixel 10 devices\",\n    \"published_at\": \"2026-05-16\",\n    \"summary\": \"Project Zero researchers demonstrated a two-bug chain enabling silent compromise and privilege escalation on Pixel 10 devices, reusing a media framework entry point and pivoting to a newly introduced /dev/vpu driver flaw to achieve kernel-level read/write primitives. Google reported patching the issue in subsequent Android security updates, highlighting ongoing risk from hardware/driver attack surface.\",\n    \"impact\": \"Zero-click device compromise can enable spyware-style outcomes: persistent malware, data theft, and full device control without user interaction.\",\n    \"recommendation\": \"Ensure devices receive patched Android security updates promptly; prioritize fleet compliance monitoring and restrict risky media handling paths where possible.\",\n    \"sources\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Cyber Security News\",\n        \"url\": \"https://cybersecuritynews.com/zero-click-exploit-chain-pixel-10-devices/\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Project Zero\",\n        \"url\": \"https://projectzero.google/2026/05/pixel-10-exploit.html\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"is_older_than_24h\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"[+24h Old] Malicious JPEG images could trigger PHP memory safety vulnerabilities\",\n    \"published_at\": \"2026-05-16\",\n    \"summary\": \"Two PHP image-processing issues were described: CVE-2025-14177 enabling heap memory disclosure via getimagesize multi-chunk APP segment handling, and a heap overflow in iptcembed due to unsafe buffer sizing (notably with FIFOs/pipes and TOCTOU growth). Crafted JPEGs can cause uninitialized memory leakage or crash/heap corruption in server-side image processing workflows.\",\n    \"impact\": \"Public upload/thumbnailing endpoints could leak sensitive process memory or suffer denial-of-service; in worst cases, memory corruption could be exploitable depending on environment hardening.\",\n    \"recommendation\": \"Upgrade PHP to fixed versions and isolate image processing; treat untrusted images as hostile and use sandboxing for metadata parsing.\",\n    \"sources\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Cyber Security News\",\n        \"url\": \"https://cybersecuritynews.com/malicious-jpeg-images-php-memory-safety-vulnerabilities/\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Positive Technologies\",\n        \"url\": \"https://swarm.ptsecurity.com/hack-the-elephant-one-bite-at-a-time-jpeg-related-memory-safety-bugs-in-php/\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"NVD CVE-2025-14177\",\n        \"url\": \"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-14177\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"is_older_than_24h\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"[+24h Old] Linux kernel flaw CVE-2026-46333 (“ssh-keysign-pwn”) exposes SSH keys and shadow passwords\",\n    \"published_at\": \"2026-05-16\",\n    \"summary\": \"CVE-2026-46333 is described as a race/logic flaw in ptrace access control and dumpability checks enabling file descriptor theft via pidfd_getfd during privileged process teardown windows. Public PoC demonstrates reading sensitive files like SSH host keys and /etc/shadow by racing privileged helpers as they exit and exploiting the mm=NULL transition state.\",\n    \"impact\": \"Local attackers can steal SSH keys and password hashes, enabling credential compromise, lateral movement, and persistent access across fleets where keys are reused.\",\n    \"recommendation\": \"Patch kernels urgently and rotate SSH host keys; monitor for abnormal pidfd_getfd usage and local privilege escalation attempts.\",\n    \"sources\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Cyber Security News\",\n        \"url\": \"https://cybersecuritynews.com/linux-kernel-vulnerability-ssh-keysign-pwn/\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"PoC (GitHub)\",\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/0xdeadbeefnetwork/ssh-keysign-pwn\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"NVD CVE-2026-46333\",\n        \"url\": \"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-46333\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"is_older_than_24h\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"[+24h Old] Claw Chain vulnerabilities put OpenClaw AI agent servers at risk (CVE-2026-44112/44113/44115/44118)\",\n    \"published_at\": \"2026-05-16\",\n    \"summary\": \"Cyera-discovered OpenClaw vulnerabilities (collectively “Claw Chain”) can be chained to escape sandbox boundaries, leak secrets (API keys/tokens), bypass ownership checks, and gain privileged control. Reporting highlights broad internet exposure of OpenClaw instances and emphasizes that agentic tooling expands the execution surface, making compromised agents difficult to distinguish from legitimate activity.\",\n    \"impact\": \"Attackers can turn privileged AI agents into internal operators (“hands inside the environment”), enabling stealthy data access and persistent backdoors.\",\n    \"recommendation\": \"Patch immediately, rotate secrets reachable by agents, and place agent servers behind authentication/segmentation with robust IAM controls.\",\n    \"sources\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Hackread\",\n        \"url\": \"https://hackread.com/claw-chain-vulnerabilities-openclaw-ai-servers-risk/\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Cyera\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.cyera.com/blog/claw-chain-cyera-research-unveil-four-chainable-vulnerabilities-in-openclaw\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"is_older_than_24h\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"[+24h Old] Avada Builder WordPress plugin flaws allow file read and SQL injection (CVE-2026-4782, CVE-2026-4798)\",\n    \"published_at\": \"2026-05-15T11:56:00-04:00\",\n    \"summary\": \"Two vulnerabilities in Avada Builder were disclosed: an authenticated arbitrary file read (subscriber-level) and an unauthenticated SQL injection path under certain WooCommerce usage conditions. Attackers could extract wp-config.php and database credentials or potentially exfiltrate data from the database, with large install base increasing exploitation interest.\",\n    \"impact\": \"Can lead to WordPress admin compromise, database credential theft, and full site takeover, especially on sites allowing user registration.\",\n    \"recommendation\": \"Upgrade Avada Builder to the fully patched release and audit for suspicious user accounts and database access patterns.\",\n    \"sources\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"BleepingComputer\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/avada-builder-wordpress-plugin-flaws-allow-site-credential-theft/\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Wordfence\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.wordfence.com/blog/2026/05/1000000-wordpress-sites-affected-by-arbitrary-file-read-and-sql-injection-vulnerabilities-in-avada-builder-wordpress-plugin/\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"is_older_than_24h\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"[+24h Old] Windows BitLocker zero-days: YellowKey encryption bypass and GreenPlasma privilege escalation\",\n    \"published_at\": \"2026-05-14\",\n    \"summary\": \"A researcher published exploit material for two Windows issues: YellowKey, a BitLocker bypass targeting WinRE workflows on newer Windows/Server versions, and GreenPlasma, a local privilege escalation concept involving service/object manipulation. The reporting emphasizes urgent mitigations given patch uncertainty and the realistic risk from physical-access scenarios for YellowKey.\",\n    \"impact\": \"Physical attackers may bypass disk encryption on targeted configurations, and local attackers may gain elevated privileges depending on exploit maturity and chaining.\",\n    \"recommendation\": \"Strengthen physical security, require BitLocker pre-boot authentication where feasible, and monitor WinRE/EFI partition integrity until patched.\",\n    \"sources\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Cyber Security News\",\n        \"url\": \"https://cybersecuritynews.com/windows-bitlocker-0-day-vulnerability/\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"YellowKey PoC (GitHub)\",\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/Nightmare-Eclipse/YellowKey\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"GreenPlasma PoC (GitHub)\",\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/Nightmare-Eclipse/GreenPlasma\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"is_older_than_24h\": true\n  }\n]